{"title":"Career Roadmap · Device Characterisation Engineer","role":"Device Characterisation Engineer","summary":"A Device Characterisation Engineer evaluates the electrical, physical, thermal, optical and reliability behaviour of semiconductor devices and micro/nanoelectronic structures. The role connects device physics, semiconductor fabrication, measurement systems, instrumentation, data analysis and failure analysis.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Micro & Nano Electronics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Device Characterisation Engineer evaluates the electrical, physical, thermal, optical and reliability behaviour of semiconductor devices and micro/nanoelectronic structures. The role connects device physics, semiconductor fabrication, measurement systems, instrumentation, data analysis and failure analysis."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical devices include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MOSFETs and CMOS devices"},{"text":"Diodes and BJTs"},{"text":"FinFETs and gate-all-around devices"},{"text":"Wide-bandgap devices such as SiC/GaN"},{"text":"MEMS/NEMS devices"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Photodetectors"},{"text":"Non-volatile memory devices"},{"text":"2D-material and nanoscale devices"},{"text":"Semiconductor process test structures"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate profile should combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Semiconductor Device Physics","Electrical Characterisation","Semiconductor Processing","Measurement Instrumentation","Data Analysis","Reliability","Python/MATLAB","Failure Analysis"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech/B.E. Micro & Nano Electronics"},{"text":"Device physics, semiconductor fabrication, electronics, measurement and data analysis"}],[{"tex